### 5. Complexity Evaluation

| Complexity Dimension | What Makes It Hard | Level |
|---|---|---|
| **Inter-Contract Communication (ICC)** | Job contract calls Escrow contract via `env.invoke_contract` — requires precise cross-contract initialization, shared state coordination, and atomic execution | 🔴 High |
| **State Machine Management** | 7 job statuses × 4 milestone statuses = 28 valid state transitions that must be enforced at the contract level with `require_auth()` | 🔴 High |
| **Multi-Wallet Integration** | Supporting Freighter, xBull, and Albedo via StellarWalletsKit with graceful fallbacks for each | 🟡 Medium |
| **Real-Time Event Streaming** | Polling Soroban contract events from the RPC layer, parsing `ScVal` topics, and rendering live activity feeds | 🟡 Medium |
| **Transaction Lifecycle** | Build → Simulate → Assemble → Sign → Submit → Poll — 6-step async pipeline with error handling at each stage | 🟡 Medium |
| **[L4] Production Hardening** | Error boundaries, loading skeletons, mobile responsive, monitoring, CI/CD with contract deploy | 🟡 Medium |
| **[L5] Reputation System** | On-chain reputation scoring based on job completion rate, dispute history — new contract with ICC to Job | 🔴 High |
| **[L6] Fee Sponsorship** | Implementing Stellar fee bump transactions so new users never pay gas — requires a fee-sponsor account | 🔴 High |
| **[L6] Multi-signature Escrow** | High-value jobs requiring M-of-N approval before escrow release — extends escrow contract significantly | 🔴 High |
| **[L6] Mainnet Security** | Smart contract audit, input validation hardening, reentrancy guards, storage optimization | 🔴 High |

